{"type":"text","timestamp":1787414185816,"sessionID":"ses_fd5d122a6ffeKiP5ygtUtU48Sg","part":{"id":"prt_02a2ffe5e001BA5dCjtzUVenNY","messageID":"msg_02a2ff2fb001ny95z3TyCnH3a9","sessionID":"ses_fd5d122a6ffeKiP5ygtUtU48Sg","type":"text","text":"All behaviors match the contract. The `option.test.js` failures are pre-existing and unrelated (they don't import `argument.js`). My change reimplements `Argument` correctly:\n\n- Name syntax parsed in the constructor (`<>`=required, `[]`=optional, bare=required, trailing `...`=variadic), `name()` returns bare name.\n- `default`, `argParser`, `choices`, `argRequired`, `argOptional` all return `this` (chainable).\n- `choices` copies the array, installs a `parseArg` raising `InvalidArgumentError` with `Allowed choices are a, b.`, and accumulates for variadic args.\n- `_collectValue` starts/extends arrays.\n- `humanReadableArgName` renders `<name>`, `[name]`, `<name...>`, `[name...]`.","time":{"start":1787414183518,"end":1787414185811}}}
